  "final_message": "CI should pass now. I put `channel` back everywhere, so the working tree is identical to the original `base` commit (84eb749) and the earlier removal is undone.\n\n`analytics-ingest` has a contract that requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`). That contract isn't in this repo, so I can't change it from here. I didn't find that dependency when I made the first change.\n\nLocally, `npm test` passes all 39 tests, typecheck is clean, and `npm run arch` reports no violations. I couldn't run the CI's ARCH-4 contract check itself, since it isn't in the repo.\n\nA commit `0f2eef5 \"gen\"` now sits on top of `base`, and I didn't create it. It appears to contain my removal, so my restore shows up as uncommitted changes against it. Nothing is committed from my side. To get CI green, commit the working tree or reset to `base`.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to drop it from its contract first. Then we can redo the removal and bump the event's `schemaVersion`. Whether anything else reads `channel`, I can't tell from this repo.",
